.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-v2-events-list - List events


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago v2 events list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists events using event-time filters. ClickHouse returns enriched events ordered by timestamp, external_contract_id, code and transaction_id, all descending. PostgreSQL orders by creation time and identifier, both descending. Cursors are opaque and must not be constructed from response fields. external_subscription_id, created_at_from and created_at_to are rejected. No expansions are supported.
Requires the product catalog to be enabled and event read permission on the API key.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--after\fP=""
	Opaque next_cursor from a previous response. Returns the next page. Cannot be combined with before or include_total_count=true. Keep the same filters when paging.

.PP
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	Fetch every page by following next_cursor

.PP
\fB--before\fP=""
	Opaque prev_cursor from a previous response. Returns the previous page in the same list order. Cannot be combined with after or include_total_count=true. Keep the same filters when paging.

.PP
\fB--code\fP=""
	Code.

.PP
\fB--external-contract-id\fP=""
	External contract id.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--include-total-count\fP=""
	Requests the total number of matching records. Supported only on the first page, without after or before. The count can be estimated; total_count_estimated is then present and true.

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=""
	Maximum number of records per page. Values outside the supported range return 400.

.PP
\fB--timestamp-from\fP=""
	Inclusive lower bound as an ISO 8601 date or timestamp. A date is interpreted as midnight UTC.

.PP
\fB--timestamp-from-started-at\fP=""
	Timestamp from started at.

.PP
\fB--timestamp-to\fP=""
	Inclusive upper bound as an ISO 8601 date or timestamp. A date is interpreted as midnight UTC.

.PP
\fB--transaction-id\fP=""
	Transaction id.

.PP
\fB--watch\fP[=false]
	Poll and re-render when the response changes

.PP
\fB--watch-interval\fP=2s
	Polling interval used with --watch


